Z||000004||rockcrawl||04-02-2001||05:27 PM||||Terry, Are you sure that is the correct # for a manual trans? I think that's for the auto. I have 14089201 listed for '88 2.8 manual. Anyway, the 88 Fiero trans is way to expensive ~ $170. Try # 14078772 from a v6 5spd Beretta. It will be much cheaper. Any 88 or newer 2.8 or 3.1 FWD flywheel will work. I got one fron the junk yard for $16, I think the GM price is like $70. It's the same weight and dimensions as an '85-'87 2.8 Fiero flywheel but it is neutrally ballanced. I don't have an '88 Fiero flywheel to compare it to. The 3.4 TDC may also work, but it is less common.<P>Jon||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||04-02-2001||05:32 PM||||I'll look again in the book, but I'm pretty sure that was marked MT. The 22P explodes the flywheel, clutches, and flexplates in different places.<P>If I can find my DOHC flyhweel, I'll get the pn for you too. <P>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||04-02-2001||10:17 PM||||Checked again.<P>According to the 22P book, page 0-42 "1984-1988 P Clutch Cover & Plate", Group 0.666, item 3, the manual trans flywheels are:<P>2.5L R all years 10044408<BR>2.8L 9 84-87 476575 (standard 660 flywheel)<BR>2.8L 9 88 only 14100554<P>Trying to figure out where I *stored* the DOHC flywheel.||||reg||1
